WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:09.290
(mellow music)

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.050
- There's this belief
that the United States

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.057
is the best place in the
entire world to have a baby

00:00:14.057 --> 00:00:16.537
and that's not true.

00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:20.254
It's the most dangerous
place in the developed world.

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:23.164
My name is Michelle
Hartney, I live in Chicago,

00:00:23.164 --> 00:00:24.664
and I'm an artist.

00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:37.286
A lot of people don't know that
our maternal mortality rate

00:00:37.286 --> 00:00:41.453
in the United States has
increased 160% since 1995.

00:00:45.394 --> 00:00:47.756
Many of our routine practices like

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:50.586
continuous monitoring and forcing mothers

00:00:50.586 --> 00:00:52.788
to give birth on their backs are not based

00:00:52.788 --> 00:00:54.705
on scientific evidence.

00:00:56.758 --> 00:00:58.858
There are still a lot of doctors that are

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.525
not doing what's best for women.

00:01:03.172 --> 00:01:06.194
I'm a approaching these
issues with my art.

00:01:06.194 --> 00:01:08.863
Art can hit you deeper than just reading

00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:11.030
a statistic on a page can.

00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:19.325
I started a series called Mother's Right.

00:01:19.325 --> 00:01:23.080
I spent the summer sewing
1,200 hospital gowns,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.247
one for every woman who died
during childbirth in 2013.

00:01:28.248 --> 00:01:31.626
The fabric of the gowns is made
up of the plant derivatives

00:01:31.626 --> 00:01:34.054
of the drugs that have
been used on laboring women

00:01:34.054 --> 00:01:35.971
for the past 150 years.

00:01:37.137 --> 00:01:41.185
We had a performance at
Daley Plaza in Chicago.

00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:44.654
The performance included pairs
of women folding the gowns

00:01:44.654 --> 00:01:47.803
into the shape of a
flag similar to the way

00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:51.512
the flag is folded at
the funeral of a soldier.

00:01:51.512 --> 00:01:54.743
To also bring awareness
to the number of women

00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:57.239
who are coming out of
childbirth with the same

00:01:57.239 --> 00:01:59.554
psychological symptoms as men and women

00:01:59.554 --> 00:02:01.574
who are fighting wars.

00:02:01.574 --> 00:02:05.260
What inspired me really
was the birth experience

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.843
of my second child.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:10.178
I mean ultimately both
of my birth experiences

00:02:10.178 --> 00:02:12.881
were empowering, but there
were things that happened

00:02:12.881 --> 00:02:17.395
during the birth of my son
that just didn't feel right.

00:02:17.395 --> 00:02:19.964
Lie on your back, those are my words that

00:02:19.964 --> 00:02:23.499
my doctor told me when I
was trying to give birth

00:02:23.499 --> 00:02:28.040
on my side and they were trying
to get me to lie on my back.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.765
Doctors should know that you can

00:02:29.765 --> 00:02:32.083
push a baby out on your side.

00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:34.453
I was with experts.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:38.368
So that's where Birth Words came from.

00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:40.443
A lot of the phrases are

00:02:40.443 --> 00:02:42.350
really disturbing, but
they're actually things

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.679
that doctors were saying to their patients

00:02:45.679 --> 00:02:48.442
while they were giving birth.

00:02:48.442 --> 00:02:50.998
And I've had people
think that I made them up

00:02:50.998 --> 00:02:53.783
because it's hard to believe that a doctor

00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:56.235
would say "suck it up and get over it"

00:02:56.235 --> 00:03:00.157
or "if you don't shut up
we will knock you out."

00:03:00.157 --> 00:03:03.509
My artwork is not trying
to say that doctors are bad

00:03:03.509 --> 00:03:05.259
or hospitals are bad.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.710
What I'm trying to say is that

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.712
women need to know that
they need to be informed

00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:14.904
when they're going into childbirth.

00:03:14.904 --> 00:03:17.909
I want my daughter, if she has a baby to

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:22.172
be giving birth in different
circumstances than we are now.

00:03:22.172 --> 00:03:25.758
Women have a choice, and that
knowledge can change the way

00:03:25.758 --> 00:03:29.925
that we are experiencing
childbirth in the United States.

